<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh Thai Aluminium 95 net up 59 pct. [CORRECTED 01:20 GMT 13/9]</title>
<headline>Bangladesh Thai Aluminium 95 net up 59 pct. [CORRECTED 01:20 GMT 13/9]</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31,</p>
<p>1995.</p>
<p>(In million taka unless stated)</p>
<p>				    1995		1994</p>
<p>(Corrects comparative year from 1996).</p>
<p>Net profit before</p>
<p>    tax holiday reserves    15.25     vs    9.58</p>
<p>    Operating net profit    23.28     vs   10.06</p>
<p>    Gross profit		65.69     vs   45.04</p>
<p>    Sales			226.44     vs  168.61</p>
<p>    Dividend	 17 taka per 100-taka share vs 15 taka</p>
<p>Note: Bangladesh Thai Aluminium (BTA) held its annual general meeting on Thursday. It said despite political unrest the company could make higher profit by raising production and sales.</p>
</text>
